      "kp_id": "e-12398"
    },
    "q-161574": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161574",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y{z}^{2}}\\frac{12}{z}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,1\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2y}\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y{z}^{2}}\\frac{12}{z}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{12}{z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=y{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{12}{z}(y{z}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12yz\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}12yz\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2y}}12yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[6y{z}^{2}]_{z=1}^{z=\\sqrt{2y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}6y((\\sqrt{2y})^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}6y(2y-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}12{y}^{2}-6y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[4{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =4(8-1)-3(4-1) \\\\  & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
