    "q-161561": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161561",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}4xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{4-2y}\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}4xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}[2z{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2z({z}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2y}}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{4-2y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{4-2y)})^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(4-2y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(16-16y+4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8-8y+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[8y-4{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =16-16+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
