    "q-161568": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161568",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{y+z}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le y\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{y+z}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}[{x}^{2}]_{x=y}^{x=y+z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+z)^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2yz+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2yz+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2yz+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[y{z}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{4}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(16-1) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-161568-a",
