    "q-161580": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161580",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2xyz\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le y+z\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the line $z=y$ in the first quadrant.",
      "worked_solution": "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2xyz\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}yz[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=y+z}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}yz(y+z)^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}yz({y}^{2}+2yz+{z}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14216491/assets/5974f852ba8dcaf9e6c4d6323709987c590e2f739524e012545738bc4bb842b0.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}{z}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}y{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}\\cdot {y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}y\\cdot {y}^{4}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{17}{12}{y}^{5}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{5}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}{[\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{6}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}(\\frac{1}{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{72}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
