    "q-161578": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161578",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-y-z\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}2\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}2\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}2\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[2x]_{x=0}^{x=4-y-z}dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2(4-y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-2z\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-2z\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-2z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[8z-2yz-{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-1\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}7-2y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}7-2y\\,dy & ={[7y-{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =7-1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
