    "q-40208": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40208",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le z\\sqrt{3}\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axes, the line $y=2$ and the line $z=y$ in the first quadrant.",
      "worked_solution": "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z\\sqrt{3}}2y\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z\\sqrt{3}}2y\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}2y[x]_{x=0}^{x=z\\sqrt{3}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2yz\\sqrt{3}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14216491/assets/63a8768b2769fad339ba7667357812d2dda0ea856e846ad666a100f8bc1336e9.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2yz\\sqrt{3}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2yz\\sqrt{3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}2z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{3}[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{3}({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{16}{4}-0) \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
