      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14216491/assets/d5690bff5819d72cc9d49016c119dc79f62f4d766c142a43a89df196ce9f2335.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14216491/assets/2427e053c0e2d808b32db5d7fedf81365e7e50f0b3f2dc61598ad1795394686e.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14216491/assets/145f0d494ffe24de84e3a289b3a7316d3f4933f193d734aed118609f7fb9f94f.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2+2y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}(2+2y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{y}^{2}z+2{y}^{3}z-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
